<title>HONG KONG: KEXIM global bond seen launching this week.</title>
<headline>KEXIM global bond seen launching this week.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Export-Import Bank of Korea (KEXIM) is expected to launch its US$500 million global bond issue this week, syndicate sources said.</p>
<p>The bond will have an intermediate maturity, probably of five years, they said.</p>
<p>Salomon Brothers and Morgan Stanley are joint lead managers.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6371</p>
</text>
